**Experiment 26: EMA of model weights**

- **What**: Maintain an exponential moving average (decay=0.995) of all model parameters during training. Use EMA weights for final evaluation instead of the raw last-step weights.
- **Why**: All "more steps via less compute" ideas are exhausted. The model is severely undertrained (~830 steps) with ~0.003 variance between identical runs. EMA smooths out SGD noise, capturing the best of the convergence trajectory. Universally proven technique (diffusion, ViT, GANs).
- **Changes**: 6 lines added — EMA init after compile, EMA update after optimizer step, EMA swap before eval.
- **Risk**: Minimal. ~220MB extra VRAM, ~1-2ms/step overhead. No architectural changes. Worst case: neutral (warmdown already converges cleanly).
